# Fixed 2026-10-01, defect 144, lane emit: the half of the rule that refuses.
# Each C type below has a value an `i64` result cannot hold, on every
# platform this compiler runs on, so its binding is refused at `build`, exit 1,
# `ffi_return_type`, on its own line. Defect 144 widened what a result may
# be to every type that holds all of C's values; these are the pairs the
# widening must still refuse, so a rule that lets one through goes red here.
# A pair whose verdict is the platform's is measured, not held
# (`tests/golden/run/fixedbugs-144-every-wider-result-builds.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-144-results.h"
    function ullong_as_i64() -> i64  #~ ffi_return_type
    function float_as_i64() -> i64  #~ ffi_return_type
    function double_as_i64() -> i64  #~ ffi_return_type
    function ldouble_as_i64() -> i64  #~ ffi_return_type

function main()
    print(1)
